  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual message",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text 'perfect girls don't exi' (intended to be 'exist'), which serves as the central claim of the meme. The text acts as a direct address to the viewer, inviting them to internalize the misogynistic message that 'perfect' women do not exist, thereby framing the user as someone who must confront or accept this notion. The text is the primary locus of the user's projection, as it explicitly states the meme's core argument and is juxtaposed with the visual material to reinforce its message.",
